import L4Factoidal.WasmVM.Hosts.LeanJS
import L4Factoidal.WasmVM.Hosts.LeanJSRealmData

/-!
# BubblePopJS's realm, made at build time

The page objects of `prelude.js` are the same for every page, so the heap the prelude
leaves is made once, when the engine is built: `lake exe bubblepop-realm` runs the prelude
(`LeanJS.prepareSource`) and writes that heap as data (`JS.Snapshot`) into
`LeanJSRealmData.lean` (generated by `labs/demos/foafnaut/build-web-render.sh`, not kept in
git). The first page of a session then decodes the heap (`prepare`): it does not lex,
parse or run the prelude.

The data is refused when it was made from another prelude (its mark is the prelude's
hash) or on another fresh realm (an engine change); `prepare` then runs the prelude, and
the check `WasmVM/Tests/LeanJSRealm.lean` fails the build, so stale data is never used
quietly.
-/
namespace L4Factoidal.WasmVM.Hosts.LeanJS

/-- The realm with the page objects: decoded from the data made at build time, or (data
refused) made by running the prelude. -/
def prepare (lim : Page.Limits := {}) : Except String Session :=
  match prepareWith realmData lim with
  | .ok s => .ok s
  | .error _ => prepareSource lim

end L4Factoidal.WasmVM.Hosts.LeanJS
